  "result": "Before anything gets built, I need to know where the cancellation news will come from. I read through the app: the timetable page is built entirely from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and the site has no warning feature yet. A nightly file also means a cancellation decided that morning wouldn't reach the site until the next day.\n\nSo the source of the information decides most of what gets built. It could be a change to the office's export, something staff update during the day, or a feed from somewhere else. Each of those leads to a very different piece of work.\n\nWhen a sailing gets cancelled today, how does that decision happen, and who knows about it first?",
